**How to implement.** `SetParameterState`, the parameter editor and the label, notes and photo edits, as semantic messages of the constructor window (001 §P `SetParameterState`; 001 §O 'a parameter grid (state, value, bounds, σ, provenance)'; the S7.2 brief: plus label, notes and photo edits, writes through KitProxy). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) Before the model: `ParameterStateChoice` = `KnownStateChoice` | `UnknownStateChoice`, the two states a user sets by hand (a calibration comes from a fit, S11.5). `ParameterEditField` = `ValueEditField` | `LowerEditField` | `UpperEditField` | `PriorSigmaEditField`. `ParameterEditDraft = { itemId : ItemId; name : ParameterName; choice : ParameterStateChoice; valueText : ControlCaption; lowerText : ControlCaption; upperText : ControlCaption; priorSigmaText : ControlCaption }`, the editor's typed-in texts, raw captions until `tryState` reads them. `static member ofParameter (itemId : ItemId) (parameter : Parameter) : ParameterEditDraft` fills it from the state: a known value is `KnownStateChoice` with that value; an unknown is `UnknownStateChoice` with its start, its bounds and its prior's sigma, the sigma empty without a prior; a calibration is `KnownStateChoice` with its value; a field the state has no number for is empty; numbers are written `ToString("R", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`. `member this.withFieldText (field : ParameterEditField) (text : ControlCaption) : ParameterEditDraft` sets one field. `member this.tryState : Result<ParameterState, ItemError>` reads the texts with `Double.TryParse(text, NumberStyles.Float, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`: `KnownStateChoice` is `KnownParameter` of the value; `UnknownStateChoice` is `UnknownParameter { start = value; bounds = { lower; upper }; priorOpt }`, `priorOpt` `None` for an empty sigma and otherwise `Some { centre = value; sigma }`, so a prior is centred on the start; a text a needed number does not read from is `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming the parameter and the field (`value`, `lower`, `upper` or `prior sigma`). The rules of a state stay `Parameter.validate`'s (step 214), which `withParameterState` applies. (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `parameterEditOpt : ParameterEditDraft option` after `addItemFormOpt` (step 239), documented in one line; `initWith` sets it to `None`, and `SelectKitItem` (step 239) sets it to `None`. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `SetParameterState of ItemId * ParameterName * ParameterState` (001 §P: the editor's Set, and how a test sets a state), `EditItemParameter of ParameterName` (a press of a parameter row of the selected item), `SetParameterEditChoice of ParameterStateChoice`, `SetParameterEditText of ParameterEditField * ControlCaption`, `CancelParameterEdit`, `RelabelKitItem of ItemId * ItemLabel`, `SetKitItemNotes of ItemId * ItemNotes`, `SetKitItemPhoto of ItemId * FileName` (the photo file the picker answered) and `RemoveKitItemPhoto of ItemId`. (4) Arms. `EditItemParameter name` opens `ParameterEditDraft.ofParameter` of the selected item's parameter of that name and changes nothing without one; `SetParameterEditChoice` and `SetParameterEditText` change the open draft (`withFieldText`) and `CancelParameterEdit` closes it; none of these writes. The six others are write messages: each goes through step 185's read-only guard first, and an id `kitItems` does not hold changes nothing. Each makes the edited item through a Domain member: `SetParameterState (id, name, state)` through `withParameterState name state` (step 234), `RelabelKitItem` through `relabelledAmong label model.kitItems` (step 236), `SetKitItemNotes` through `withNotes`, `RemoveKitItemPhoto` through `withPhoto None`, and `SetKitItemPhoto (id, file)` through `model.experimentData.attachDataFile file` (step 135: a file inside the kit is recorded in place, one outside is copied into `data/`) and then `withPhoto (Some attachment.path)`. A refusal sets `kitStatus` to `The item was not changed — <e.describe>`, or `The photo was not attached — <e.describe>` for the attach, and writes nothing more. The edited item is then recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }`: `recordRelabelledItem item edited` (step 237) for a relabel, `recordItem edited` (step 219) otherwise. `Ok ()` replaces the item in `kitItems` in label order, closes the editor after a `SetParameterState` and sets `kitStatus` to `None`; `Error e` keeps `kitItems` and sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. No undo, publish (S11.5) or dial edit is added: the dial is chosen when the item is added (step 215). Tests, in `ItemsPanelModelTests` (step 239), over its model holding CPL1, added through `AddItem` of step 239's CPL1 draft (the circular-polarizer model, `DialMounted DialPositive`): `SetParameterState sets an item's parameter and records it`: `SetParameterState` of CPL1's `c2.retardance` as `UnknownParameter` starting at π / 2 within [π / 4, 3π / 4] leaves that state in `kitItems` and in `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()`, at revision 1. `a parameter state that breaks its rules is told and nothing is recorded`: the same with the bounds reversed sets `kitStatus` containing `the parameter state is not valid`, and `kitItems` and `readItems ()` are unchanged. `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets`: `EditItemParameter (ParameterName "c2.retardance")` opens a draft at `KnownStateChoice` whose value text reads back π / 2 exactly; `SetParameterEditChoice UnknownStateChoice` with the lower, upper and prior-sigma texts `0.7`, `2.4` and `0.1` gives a `tryState` of an unknown starting at π / 2 within [0.7, 2.4] with a prior centred at π / 2 of sigma 0.1; the lower text `abc` gives `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming `lower`; an empty sigma gives no prior; `ofParameter` of a calibration of 1.55 is `KnownStateChoice` at 1.55; `CancelParameterEdit` closes the draft. `relabelling an item renames its kit file, and a label another item holds is told`: `RelabelKitItem` of CPL1 to `CPL 1` leaves `kitItems` labelled `CPL 1` and the kit's item files `CPL 1.item-json` alone; with LP1 added, relabelling `CPL 1` to `lp1` sets `kitStatus` containing `already has an item of that label`. `notes and a photo are recorded with the item, and removing the photo keeps its file`: `SetKitItemNotes` of `Mounted` is read back by `readItems ()`; `SetKitItemPhoto` of a file the fact writes under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "ItemsPanelModelTests", <a new GUID>, "CPL1.jpg")` gives CPL1 the photo `data/CPL1.jpg`, which the kit's `paths` hold; `RemoveKitItemPhoto` removes the photo and `data/CPL1.jpg` stays. `a kit opened read-only edits no item and writes nothing`: over the read-only model of step 239's fact with `kitItems` set to the CPL1 the scratch kit holds, each of the six write messages sets `kitStatus` to the read-only text and the kit's `paths` are unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the edit messages land, `SetParameterState`, `RelabelKitItem`, `SetKitItemNotes`, `SetKitItemPhoto` and `RemoveKitItemPhoto` MUST change one item through its Domain member and record it, telling a refusal and writing nothing under a read-only kit, and `ParameterEditDraft.tryState` MUST read the state the editor sets; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SetParameterState sets an item's parameter and records it`, `a parameter state that breaks its rules is told and nothing is recorded`, `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets`, `relabelling an item renames its kit file, and a label another item holds is told`, `notes and a photo are recorded with the item, and removing the photo keeps its file` and `a kit opened read-only edits no item and writes nothing`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.
